  "name": "interval-heap",
  "description": "A Rust implementation of a double-ended priority queue (DEPQ) leveraging the interval heap data structure for efficient dual-end extremum management. The library facilitates O(1) access and O(log n) mutation for both minimum and maximum elements by organizing a binary tree where each node encapsulates a closed interval containing its descendants. It is engineered for no_std environments and supports arbitrary ordering logic via externalized comparators.",
